WEBVTT

00:05.390 --> 00:06.360
Hey! Hey!

00:06.360 --> 00:07.970
What story will you tell me tonight?

00:09.010 --> 00:12.030
What about the time 
I visited a very salty and large pond? {Note: Pretty sure this is Holo.}

00:12.030 --> 00:13.740
You already told me that story.

00:13.740 --> 00:18.370
Then, what about the time 
I bit the arse of a pompous fool?

00:18.370 --> 00:20.080
You've told me that one, too.

00:20.080 --> 00:21.840
I don't want to hear those childish stories.

00:21.840 --> 00:24.370
Aren't there any stories 
I've never heard before?

00:24.370 --> 00:30.250
Then, what about an old tale from long ago, 
that began in a village far, far away?

00:30.250 --> 00:33.520
It's a story about a wolf 
that protected the harvests of a village

00:33.520 --> 00:37.140
in a land much farther south than here...

00:37.140 --> 00:38.520
A wolf?

00:38.520 --> 00:42.490
The wolf promised the youths of that village

00:42.490 --> 00:45.410
that it would bring 
bountiful harvests of wheat.

00:45.410 --> 00:47.860
The wolf kept its promise.

00:48.300 --> 00:52.530
It kept it for an exceedingly long time.

00:52.850 --> 00:54.640
No one knows when it began,

00:54.640 --> 00:57.780
but the people of the village 
would use the phrase "the wolf is running"

00:57.780 --> 01:00.720
when ripe wheat stalks swayed in the wind.

01:00.720 --> 01:02.740
When ears of wheat were flattened by the wind,

01:02.740 --> 01:04.660
they said they were "trampled by the wolf".

01:04.660 --> 01:08.290
They even said the wheat was "eaten by 
the wolf" when the harvest was poor.

01:08.290 --> 01:11.420
The village must have 
really treasured that wolf.

01:11.420 --> 01:12.240
Yes...

01:12.240 --> 01:13.520
Yes, they did.

01:13.520 --> 01:15.290
So, they all lived happily ever after?

01:15.290 --> 01:17.300
That's the end of the story?

01:17.300 --> 01:18.150
No...

01:18.590 --> 01:20.820
After a long time had passed,

01:20.820 --> 01:24.930
no one remembered the promise 
they made with the wolf anymore.

01:25.490 --> 01:29.460
The tales of the wolf, 
which were full of familiarity and awe,

01:29.460 --> 01:32.820
eventually just became antiquated stories.

01:33.370 --> 01:37.730
The humans who began to sow, nurture, 
and harvest the wheat themselves

01:37.730 --> 01:42.380
no longer believed in the wolf 
that brought bountiful harvests...

01:42.900 --> 01:45.830
So, then, what happened to that wolf?

01:48.750 --> 01:52.050
Well, at the time, in the village...

01:54.340 --> 01:58.560
Spice and Wolf

01:58.560 --> 01:59.680
Spice and Wolf

01:59.680 --> 02:05.020
Spice and Wolf

03:38.300 --> 03:40.740
The clear weather 
should last until nightfall again.

03:40.900 --> 03:45.410
<b>Episode 1
The Harvest Festival and 
The Crowded Driver's Box</b>

03:41.420 --> 03:43.730
Wouldn't rain be troublesome for you, too?

03:51.190 --> 03:52.250
A traveling merchant?

03:52.830 --> 03:56.680
There's a small village in the mountains 
about a half a day's travel east from here.

03:56.680 --> 03:59.090
I'm on my way back after selling some salt.

03:59.090 --> 04:00.670
What kind of cargo do you have there?

04:03.170 --> 04:04.220
Fur pelts.

04:04.220 --> 04:05.330
I see.

04:05.330 --> 04:06.200
What's this?

04:06.200 --> 04:08.180
A sheaf of wheat I received from the village.

04:08.550 --> 04:11.940
I hear it's a variety of wheat that's strong 
against the cold and resilient against pests.

04:13.340 --> 04:14.770
What's going on?

04:14.770 --> 04:17.820
There normally aren't knights 
such as yourself around these parts.

04:17.820 --> 04:22.340
There's been word of a pagan festival 
being held in the villages around here.

04:22.340 --> 04:23.570
Pagans?

04:23.570 --> 04:28.280
Heretics that don't believe in 
the great God that created our world.

04:28.280 --> 04:32.370
I understand the North, but I can't believe 
there's still some of them around here.

04:32.370 --> 04:34.140
Know anything about it?

04:35.460 --> 04:36.370
Not a thing.

04:42.350 --> 04:44.180
A pagan village, huh?

04:51.650 --> 04:54.230
Hello! Long time no see!

04:54.970 --> 04:58.900
Oh, you're...

04:58.900 --> 05:01.110
The traveling merchant, Kraft Lawrence.

05:01.110 --> 05:03.240
Looks like quite the harvest this year.

05:03.240 --> 05:05.640
That's right. Look at all of this!

05:06.380 --> 05:09.200
I've come to see Yarei. Where is he?

05:09.200 --> 05:11.600
Yarei's in the field over yonder.

05:11.600 --> 05:12.870
Thank you very much.

05:12.870 --> 05:15.620
You might miss him if you don't hurry.

05:15.620 --> 05:16.570
Huh?

05:16.570 --> 05:20.210
There's a lot of young men 
over there, and they're still lacking in skill.

05:20.210 --> 05:23.810
I'm sure one of them 
will end up as Holo this year.

05:24.540 --> 05:25.670
Holo?

05:25.670 --> 05:27.840
The wolf is there! The wolf is there!

05:28.160 --> 05:30.640
The wolf is resting there!

05:33.790 --> 05:35.520
It's the last sheaf!

05:35.850 --> 05:37.850
Careful not to cut too much!

05:38.480 --> 05:41.110
Holo will run from greedy hands!

05:41.110 --> 05:44.450
Who will catch the wolf this year?!

05:52.620 --> 05:55.430
It's Yarei! It's Yarei! It's Yarei!

05:58.370 --> 05:59.610
Holo has appeared!

05:59.610 --> 06:00.420
Yarei...

06:00.420 --> 06:02.380
Holo has appeared!

06:02.380 --> 06:03.840
Catch him!

06:13.510 --> 06:15.560
We've caught Holo!

06:15.560 --> 06:17.250
Corner him!

06:20.770 --> 06:22.610
Don't let him escape!

06:22.610 --> 06:24.690
Lock him in!

06:27.170 --> 06:28.320
Lawrence!

06:28.940 --> 06:30.100
See you later!

06:32.430 --> 06:34.660
See you later? Really?

06:40.170 --> 06:42.620
But you won't be able to come out for a week...

06:49.120 --> 06:51.560
Looks like another bountiful harvest.

06:51.560 --> 06:56.340
Yes. This is all thanks to Count Erhendott.

06:56.340 --> 06:58.180
He's the new lord of the fiefdom, isn't he?

06:58.180 --> 07:01.340
Looks like the era of praying 
to the old gods has ended.

07:02.730 --> 07:05.620
We have a bad harvest 
when the wolf is displeased.

07:05.620 --> 07:10.420
But we've no bad harvests with the new 
farming methods our lord has taught us.

07:11.290 --> 07:15.280
I never thought I'd see this much Trenni 
silver in such a rural area! What a surprise!

07:15.280 --> 07:17.900
Again, all thanks to our new lord.

07:17.900 --> 07:20.870
Is your price negotiator doing a good job?

07:20.870 --> 07:24.210
If you're talking about Yarei, 
he's doing an excellent job.

07:24.210 --> 07:28.760
He always says he learned 
how to do business from you.

07:28.760 --> 07:30.760
He's just reaping the fruits of his labor.

07:31.080 --> 07:35.100
Yarei was looking forward 
to seeing you again, Mr. Lawrence.

07:35.100 --> 07:36.620
How unfortunate.

07:36.620 --> 07:38.720
Will you stay the night tonight?

07:40.270 --> 07:41.650
Thank you very much.

07:41.650 --> 07:45.020
However, the items I've purchased 
have a payment deadline.

07:45.470 --> 07:47.210
Next time, perhaps.

07:56.490 --> 07:58.630
No point in an outsider staying here alone...

08:12.150 --> 08:15.010
Fresh vegetables. Aren't they delicious?

08:18.950 --> 08:20.020
I guess I should sleep.

08:55.820 --> 08:56.680
Hey!

08:58.980 --> 09:00.060
Wake up!

09:00.060 --> 09:01.420
Hey, you!

09:01.420 --> 09:03.250
What are you doing in another person's cart?!

09:03.810 --> 09:04.790
Hey!

09:09.630 --> 09:10.750
E-Ears?!

09:57.730 --> 09:59.300
What a beautiful moon.

09:59.300 --> 10:00.700
Do you happen to have any alcohol?

10:02.340 --> 10:03.690
I-I don't have anything like that!

10:03.690 --> 10:04.770
First of all, what on earth are—

10:04.770 --> 10:07.250
Then, something to eat...

10:08.700 --> 10:11.540
Oh? Is that dried meat?

10:11.540 --> 10:12.940
How wasteful.

10:14.760 --> 10:16.880
You! Are you the sort possessed by the devil?!

10:17.660 --> 10:20.640
You must be an ungrateful wretch 
to point your blade at me.

10:20.640 --> 10:21.880
What did you say?

10:21.880 --> 10:26.180
Oh, that's right. 
You are not a human from the village.

10:26.180 --> 10:28.750
My apologies. I had forgotten that.

10:30.020 --> 10:33.700
I slipped into your carriage 
because I wished to leave the village...

10:34.900 --> 10:36.930
It seems we have already left.

10:38.130 --> 10:39.910
My name is Holo.

10:40.650 --> 10:43.700
It has been a long time 
since I've taken this form.

10:43.700 --> 10:45.940
Yes, there seem to be no problems.

10:45.940 --> 10:46.700
Holo?

10:46.700 --> 10:49.790
Mm, Holo. Isn't it an excellent name?

10:53.170 --> 10:54.420
What a coincidence!

10:55.170 --> 10:57.670
I happen to know someone 
who's been called that name.

10:57.670 --> 10:58.970
Oh?

10:58.970 --> 11:02.690
I know of no creature with 
the name Holo other than myself.

11:02.690 --> 11:04.050
Pray tell, who has this name?

11:04.360 --> 11:07.010
It's the name of 
the god of harvest in this area.

11:07.010 --> 11:08.380
Are you a god?

11:08.380 --> 11:09.430
Hmph.

11:09.760 --> 11:14.120
Though I have been called a god 
and bound to this land for a long time,

11:14.120 --> 11:16.690
I am nothing so grand.

11:16.690 --> 11:19.610
I am only Holo and nothing more.

11:20.540 --> 11:26.740
You think of me as a strange girl who has been 
locked away at home since birth, do you?

11:26.740 --> 11:31.000
I was not born here, 
but in a land much farther north.

11:31.000 --> 11:31.960
North?

11:31.960 --> 11:35.360
Yes. The summers are short 
and the winters long.

11:35.360 --> 11:37.050
A world covered in silvery white.

11:37.690 --> 11:40.090
I was born in a place called Yoitsu...

11:40.090 --> 11:43.130
Wise Wolf Holo of Yoitsu would refer to me.

11:43.870 --> 11:45.970
Have you been there before?

11:45.970 --> 11:46.930
Yoitsu?

11:47.340 --> 11:49.850
No, I've never heard of the place...

11:52.400 --> 11:53.220
What else?

11:55.130 --> 11:58.440
While I don't dislike taking 
a human form, it is always so chilly.

12:07.090 --> 12:12.580
Hey, if you're really the Wise Wolf Holo, 
show me some proof.

12:12.580 --> 12:15.240
My ears and tail are not enough to satisfy you,

12:15.240 --> 12:18.080
so you wish for me to show you 
my form as a wolf?

12:18.080 --> 12:18.850
That's right.

12:20.420 --> 12:21.590
I refuse.

12:22.490 --> 12:23.410
Why?

12:24.840 --> 12:26.620
I wish to ask you the same thing!

12:27.010 --> 12:31.600
I-If you're a person, 
I'll turn you into the Church.

12:31.600 --> 12:33.940
Those possessed by the devil 
will bring calamity upon others.

12:33.940 --> 12:35.770
I hate the Church!

12:35.770 --> 12:38.650
Then, let's go back to the village 
and confirm with the village chief...

12:39.990 --> 12:42.490
I refuse that as well.

12:44.180 --> 12:49.080
But you can stay with me if you really 
are Holo, the god of harvest.

12:49.850 --> 12:51.280
Truly?

12:51.280 --> 12:52.160
Truly.

12:52.610 --> 12:56.710
If you're really the Wise Wolf Holo, 
you might bring me some fortune as well.

12:56.710 --> 12:58.710
You truly wish to see?

12:58.710 --> 12:59.580
Yes.

12:59.580 --> 13:00.700
No matter what?

13:00.700 --> 13:01.820
No matter what!

13:05.150 --> 13:09.510
It is impossible for any creature 
to change forms without paying a price.

13:09.510 --> 13:12.280
In my case, I would need 
blood from the living...

13:12.280 --> 13:14.850
Or a small amount of wheat.

13:15.940 --> 13:16.890
Let's go with wheat.

13:29.660 --> 13:32.110
H-Hey, are you all right?!

14:05.050 --> 14:07.060
Oh, Mr. Lawrence.

14:07.060 --> 14:08.460
My apologies.

14:08.460 --> 14:10.410
May I stay here for the night?

14:10.410 --> 14:14.370
Of course, but why the sudden change?

14:14.700 --> 14:15.690
Yarei?

14:17.900 --> 14:19.910
We meet again, Lawrence.

14:21.420 --> 14:25.590
The bed is over there. 
You can place your things around there.

14:25.590 --> 14:27.200
Thank you very much.

14:27.200 --> 14:30.010
Then, please take care of the place for us.

14:32.650 --> 14:34.440
What a luxurious meal.

14:34.440 --> 14:35.930
They're all offerings for Holo.

14:35.930 --> 14:40.900
But I brought them here since it'd be a waste 
to leave it all for the wolf. Want some?

14:40.900 --> 14:43.590
I don't think an outsider 
should eat the offerings...

14:44.230 --> 14:47.570
To begin with, aren't you supposed to be 
locked away in the granary for a week,

14:47.570 --> 14:51.370
so that Holo won't escape from 
the last sheaf of wheat you harvested?

14:51.370 --> 14:52.780
That's just a superstition.

14:52.780 --> 14:55.740
There's no wolf actually 
living in the wheat fields.

14:55.740 --> 14:59.710
It's just an excuse for the people 
in the village to have a festival.

15:00.400 --> 15:03.530
This is on me. Now, drink.

15:03.530 --> 15:04.790
To an old friend!

15:04.790 --> 15:08.340
To reuniting with Lawrence, 
the shrewd traveling merchant!

15:08.970 --> 15:09.970
To an old friend.

15:09.970 --> 15:11.640
To the future of Pasloe Village!

15:15.030 --> 15:16.930
The village chief showed me the village silver.

15:17.280 --> 15:20.140
Looks like you're doing 
a good job negotiating prices.

15:20.500 --> 15:23.490
I learned it all from you!

15:23.490 --> 15:24.710
Is that so?

15:25.510 --> 15:26.730
It is!

15:30.650 --> 15:34.610
How long has it been since I started 
buying wheat from this village?

15:35.310 --> 15:36.990
Let me think...

15:36.990 --> 15:40.750
It was before Count Erhendott became our lord.

15:41.670 --> 15:46.070
The previous lord only thought about 
taking more and more taxes from us.

15:47.920 --> 15:53.340
No merchant was willing to buy 
our expensive, tax-inflated wheat.

15:53.620 --> 15:57.050
At the time, you actually 
bought some wheat from us.

15:57.430 --> 16:01.850
There weren't many towns willing to work 
with a new traveling merchant like me.

16:01.850 --> 16:05.160
The village and I have grown a lot since then.

16:05.160 --> 16:06.560
Can you believe it?

16:06.560 --> 16:10.960
Now, even merchants from large 
towns come to buy our wheat.

16:10.960 --> 16:14.030
I'm negotiating prices 
with big shots like that!

16:14.330 --> 16:16.210
I believe it.

16:16.210 --> 16:21.650
I want to try negotiating prices of wheat 
with you again. Just like back then!

16:21.650 --> 16:22.830
Yeah.

16:23.290 --> 16:25.330
Me, too, Yarei.

16:27.710 --> 16:28.500
You know!

16:28.500 --> 16:32.360
I'm sure we'll have a great harvest 
next year and the year after that!

16:32.360 --> 16:34.900
Yeah, I hope Holo stays in a happy mood.

16:34.900 --> 16:37.060
It has nothing to do with wolves!

16:37.060 --> 16:39.140
Something like that doesn't exist!

16:39.140 --> 16:40.850
We don't need some ancient god!

16:40.850 --> 16:43.640
We can't go against the Church in this era.

16:43.640 --> 16:46.550
We don't need Holo anymore!

17:17.570 --> 17:20.680
They don't need Holo anymore, huh?

17:20.680 --> 17:22.350
What about me?

17:23.990 --> 17:26.230
There is no need to be so surprised.

17:26.230 --> 17:27.240
You!

17:27.240 --> 17:29.650
As expected, this form is quite chilly.

17:31.610 --> 17:33.400
You were in the village after all.

17:33.400 --> 17:34.940
Where were you hiding?

17:35.730 --> 17:39.320
To be precise, I live inside the wheat.

17:39.780 --> 17:43.360
During the harvest, 
I am in the last piece of wheat.

17:43.360 --> 17:45.460
That's why it's quite difficult 
to escape from there.

17:45.870 --> 17:47.580
However, there are exceptions.

17:47.580 --> 17:51.560
If there is a larger amount of wheat 
than the last sheaf of wheat nearby,

17:51.560 --> 17:54.960
I can move to that wheat 
without being seen by humans.

17:55.260 --> 17:56.930
That's the reason why.

17:56.930 --> 18:01.100
In a way, I owe you a great debt.

18:03.930 --> 18:05.810
Are you afraid of me?

18:08.790 --> 18:09.690
I...

18:16.530 --> 18:19.490
Even though I was the one who 
told you to show me your true form...

18:31.350 --> 18:34.420
I was scared of you.

18:37.660 --> 18:42.330
That's why I thought 
you disappeared from my sight.

18:45.510 --> 18:50.690
Humans show fear when they see my true form.

18:50.950 --> 18:53.700
There are very few who have reacted otherwise.

18:54.070 --> 18:57.440
There was once such a person in this village.

18:58.010 --> 19:04.030
That person asked me to ensure 
the harvests of this village.

19:05.010 --> 19:08.040
That's why I kept my promise.

19:08.040 --> 19:13.100
However, having many bountiful 
harvests is hard on the land.

19:13.710 --> 19:15.800
So, there were times 
when I had to create bad harvests.

19:16.850 --> 19:21.140
The people of the village 
just called it my fickleness.

19:21.860 --> 19:24.500
Their thoughts of me have grown 
quite bad these last few years.

19:26.010 --> 19:27.980
Next year and the year after that,

19:27.980 --> 19:31.530
I am sure that they will have 
bountiful harvests without me.

19:32.370 --> 19:35.400
No one needs me any longer.

19:36.860 --> 19:39.990
Let's say that I believe you.

19:40.690 --> 19:42.710
You are quite the suspicious one.

19:42.710 --> 19:46.140
Is there somewhere you'd like to go 
after leaving the village?

19:58.770 --> 19:59.940
North...

20:02.560 --> 20:05.090
I wish to return to the north...

20:24.300 --> 20:25.370
It's safe now.

20:25.370 --> 20:27.050
Finally!

20:28.930 --> 20:32.040
It was so dark and cramped that it was 
difficult to change my clothes.

20:33.070 --> 20:34.460
Y-You!

20:37.380 --> 20:39.420
What do you think? Does it look nice on me?

20:39.420 --> 20:41.480
Wait! Those are mine!

20:41.480 --> 20:43.420
I expected as much.

20:44.510 --> 20:46.660
Those are my best clothes. 
It took me ten years!

20:46.660 --> 20:50.390
True. It is well-tailored and made of 
excellent fabric. Quite suitable for me.

20:50.690 --> 20:53.010
It seems you are a talented merchant.

20:53.010 --> 20:54.610
Those are my clothes!

20:54.610 --> 20:58.230
Yes, but I know you are a kind male.

20:58.650 --> 21:00.900
You wouldn't tell me to 
take them off, would you?

21:02.250 --> 21:04.280
I wish to travel with you.

21:05.780 --> 21:07.050
Is that unacceptable?

21:12.540 --> 21:13.620
Fine.

21:14.540 --> 21:16.260
This must be some kind of fate.

21:17.580 --> 21:20.380
Please take care of me from now on, um...

21:20.380 --> 21:23.020
Lawrence. Kraft Lawrence.

21:23.020 --> 21:24.650
Yes. Lawrence.

21:24.650 --> 21:29.730
I will continue to speak of your greatness 
from now to the end of time.

21:29.730 --> 21:32.270
My profession isn't an easy one.

21:32.270 --> 21:34.460
You'll have to earn your own keep.

21:40.460 --> 21:44.990
I am not shameless enough to eat your food 
without doing anything in return.

21:44.990 --> 21:48.970
I am the Wise Wolf Holo, an honorable wolf!

21:56.380 --> 21:57.210
By the way.

21:59.630 --> 22:02.960
It is quite cramped 
with the two of us sitting here.

22:03.910 --> 22:05.490
Hey, now...

22:05.490 --> 22:07.000
Wha?! Hey!

22:07.000 --> 22:08.580
Hey! Don't get too close!

22:08.580 --> 22:11.070
A male should be happy to be touched by me.

22:11.070 --> 22:12.180
No, not really...

22:12.180 --> 22:14.190
Oh? It seems you are embarrassed...

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
Episode 2

23:44.980 --> 23:49.990
Mischievous Wolf and No Laughing Matter

23:45.750 --> 23:49.350
Next Time: "Mischievous Wolf and No Laughing Matter"
